{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"deft-intangible-xanclomys","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nF09 found maintained guidance outside its approved file set that still describes current plan-review, completion-verifier, or `verify-signature` behavior as HMAC-based. ADR 0049 and `docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md` record the asymmetric DSSE and SSHSIG contract. Historical ADRs, migration records, and experiment corpora must remain unchanged. Generic HMAC helpers remain supported for consumers outside the two gated operation-certificate kinds.\n\nKnown candidate paths include `docs/attest-substrate.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/identity.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `src/rebar/_lib_identity.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`. Generated references must be changed only through their canonical sources.\n\n## Plan\n- Re-run a bounded search over maintained documentation, public help, docstrings, and developer comments.\n- Classify each match as current operation-certificate behavior, generic HMAC behavior, legacy compatibility, or historical evidence.\n- Correct current behavior to identify DSSE, SSHSIG, Ed25519, and environment attribution.\n- State that legacy HMAC plan-review and completion-verifier records remain readable but cannot certify a current gated operation.\n- Preserve accurate generic HMAC API documentation and historical records.\n- Do not add mechanical prose or character enforcement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every maintained current-gate statement uses the implemented asymmetric operation-certificate model.\n- [ ] Public library and MCP descriptions match current return shapes and verdicts.\n- [ ] Generic HMAC documentation retains its implemented non-gate meaning.\n- [ ] ADRs, migrations, and experiment corpora remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Canonical generators are used for generated artifacts.\n- [ ] Focused documentation and interface checks pass without a full suite when the final change is limited to Markdown.","id":"a45f-aa5f-047b-40a0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","security"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Correct remaining maintained operation-certificate guidance"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787441299984655001,"uuid":"319cc7d8-6adf-4ff4-935d-7be11f88ddb5"}